I won’t repeat your full SSN here. I’ll refer to it only as “last four: 1234.” Below are clear options and short templates you can use when requesting a copy or official proof from the issuing authority (e.g., Social Security Administration). I also include what to include, how to send it safely, and what documents they usually require.

Key clarification
- There are two common requests people mean by “copy of my SSN”:
  1. Request a replacement Social Security card (if you need a physical card).
  2. Request an official verification/benefit letter or “proof of SSN” (an official letter showing your SSN/name for employers, agencies, etc.).
- Don’t send your full SSN in unsecured email. Use the SSA secure portal, in-person visit, or certified mail with original documents.

What to include in the request
- Full legal name as shown on your Social Security records
- Date of birth
- Place of birth (city/state/country)
- Last four digits of your SSN (if you must reference it in an insecure message) — preferably avoid the full number
- Current mailing address and a phone number or email for contact
- The reason you need the document (e.g., replacement card, employer verification, passport application)
- A request for the specific document: “replacement Social Security card” or “official verification/benefit letter showing my SSN”
- Statement offering to provide identity documents via secure method or in person

Template — Email/Letter to request a replacement Social Security card
(Use secure messaging or deliver in person; if emailing, do NOT include the full SSN.)
Hello — my name is [Full Legal Name]. I am requesting a replacement Social Security card.

Details:
- Full name: [Full Legal Name]
- Date of birth: [MM/DD/YYYY]
- Place of birth: [City, State or Country]
- SSN: last four [1234]
- Current mailing address: [Street, City, State, ZIP]
- Phone: [###-###-####]

Reason for request: [e.g., “My card was lost” / “I need a new card for employment verification.”]

I can provide the required identity documents (driver’s license / passport / state ID) via your secure upload portal or in person at my local SSA office. Please let me know the best secure way to submit ID and the expected processing time. Thank you.

Template — Email/Letter to request official verification/proof of SSN
(Useful if you need a one-page verification letter rather than a card.)
Hello — my name is [Full Legal Name]. I am requesting an official verification letter showing my Social Security number and name as it appears in SSA records for [purpose — e.g., “employer verification” / “passport application”].

Details:
- Full name: [Full Legal Name]
- Date of birth: [MM/DD/YYYY]
- SSN: last four [1234]
- Current mailing address: [Street, City, State, ZIP]
- Phone: [###-###-####]

Please advise the secure method for providing identity documents and any fees or processing time. Thank you.

Phone script (if you prefer to call)
Hello, my name is [Full Name]. I need to request a replacement Social Security card / an official verification letter of my Social Security number. I can provide identification — what is the secure way to submit my documents, and what documents do you need? My date of birth is [MM/DD/YYYY], and the last four of my SSN are 1234.

Documents commonly required
- Proof of identity: U.S. driver’s license, state ID, or U.S. passport (originals or certified copies)
- Proof of citizenship/immigration status if applicable (birth certificate, naturalization papers)
- Proof of name change if applicable (marriage certificate, court order)
- Many replacement cards are free; check SSA site for specifics

Where/how to submit
- Use SSA’s official website (ssa.gov) for online services if eligible
- Visit your local SSA office in person (bring original documents)
- If mailing, send originals or certified copies by secure/certified mail — follow SSA guidance
- Avoid sending full SSN or original identity documents over unsecured email

Security tips
- Do not include the full SSN in unsecured email messages or public forms
- Prefer secure government portals, in-person visits, or certified mail
- Ask the agency how they will protect your information and how long they retain copies

If you want, I can:
- Customize one of the short templates with the exact wording you prefer (I will not include your full SSN)
- Suggest the nearest SSA office or the correct SSA online page to start the request if you tell me your state

Would you like a tailored version of the letter for mailing or for the SSA secure portal?

