[Your signature / typed name]

Phone script (if you call)
“Hi, my name is [Full Name]. I’m calling to request a copy/verification of my Social Security record/SSN. My date of birth is [MM/DD/YYYY] and the last four digits of my SSN are 1234. Could you tell me what identification and documentation you require and the secure way to submit those documents? Also, what is the expected processing time?”

What to include or have ready
- Government-issued photo ID (driver’s license, passport, state ID) — originals are often required.  
- Proof of citizenship or lawful status if requested (birth certificate, passport, immigration documents).  
- Completed forms if needed (e.g., SSA Form SS-5 for replacement cards).  
- Current mailing address.  
- Phone number and secure contact method.  
- If mailing, use certified mail or another trackable method for original documents; if uploading, use the agency’s official secure portal only.

Security tips
- Verify phone numbers and web addresses on the official agency website before contacting.  
- Avoid sending your full SSN by unsecured email unless the agency explicitly provides a secure, encrypted upload method.  
- If you must mail sensitive documents, use tracked/certified mail and only send originals if required; ask if notarized or certified copies are acceptable.  
- Watch for phishing: authorities will not call/email asking for payment via gift cards or ask for unnecessary personal data.

Timing and fees
- Processing time and fees vary by agency and request type. For SSA card replacements, typical mailing times are about 10–14 business days after processing, but confirm with the office you contact.

Would you like:
- A version of one of the templates with placeholders filled in (I will not insert your full SSN unless you explicitly ask), or  
- A version that includes the SSN placeholder formatted the way you prefer (e.g., “[SSN: XXX-XX-1234]”), or  
- Guidance tailored to a specific authority (for example, Social Security Administration vs. a state agency)?

Tell me which template you prefer and whether to include last-four only or a placeholder for the full SSN.

