Subject: Request — Procedure to Obtain Copy/Verification of SSN Record

Hello,

I need to obtain an official copy/verification of my Social Security record (or a replacement Social Security card). Before I provide any sensitive information, could you please confirm:
1) the specific documents and forms you require from me (IDs, proof of citizenship, etc.);  
2) the secure methods you accept for submitting identity documents and my SSN (secure portal, in‑person, certified mail, etc.); and  
3) any fees, forms, or expected processing time.

My identifying details:
- Full name: [Your full legal name]  
- Date of birth: [MM/DD/YYYY]  

Please let me know the next steps and the secure way to transmit my SSN or other required sensitive data. Thank you.

Sincerely,  
[Your name]  
[Phone number]  
[Mailing address]

Formal request letter (if you need to mail or provide a signed letter)
[Date]

To Whom It May Concern,

I am requesting an official copy/verification of my Social Security record (or replacement Social Security card). Please advise what documentation you require and how I should submit my identity documents and SSN securely. I am prepared to provide the following identifying information and copies of identification upon request:

- Full legal name: [Your full name]  
- Date of birth: [MM/DD/YYYY]  
- Place of birth: [City, State, Country]  
- Current address: [Your address]  
- Telephone: [Your phone]

Please provide:
- A list of required documents and acceptable forms of ID  
- The preferred secure submission method (in-person, secure online portal, or certified mail)  
- Any applicable forms/fees and processing times

Thank you for your assistance. Please confirm receipt of this request and the next steps.

Sincerely,  
[Your signature if mailing]  
[Your printed name]

Phone script (if you call)
“Hi, my name is [Name]. I need to request a copy/verification of my Social Security record or a replacement card. Before I give any sensitive numbers, could you tell me the documents you require and how you accept SSNs or ID documents securely? Also, are there any forms, fees, or expected processing times I should be aware of?”

Document checklist (commonly requested)
- Government photo ID (driver’s license, passport)  
- Proof of U.S. citizenship or immigration status if applicable (birth certificate, naturalization)  
- Proof of current address (utility bill, bank statement)  
- Completed form if required by the agency (e.g., SSA form for replacement card)  
- Any additional identity documents the office asks for

Security tips
- Don’t send your full SSN in an unsecured email. Ask for their secure upload portal, encrypted email instructions, or to provide the SSN in person.  
- Use the issuing authority’s official website or phone number (e.g., ssa.gov or your local SSA office) to confirm procedures.  
- If mailing documents, use certified mail with tracking and keep copies for your records.  
- Ask for an acknowledgement of receipt and a point of contact.

If you want, tell me:
- Which agency/office you need to contact (e.g., Social Security Administration, a state agency, employer), and  
- Whether you want a short email, formal letter, or phone script filled in with your details (I will NOT insert your full SSN; I can include a placeholder like “[last 4 digits: 1234]” if you want to indicate the last four).

