- Ask for a “certified” or “official” verification letter if you need it for legal or government purposes. Specify delivery method (secure mail, in-person pickup, or secure portal).  
- Processing times vary; ask for an estimated timeline.

Security and privacy tips
- Avoid sending your full SSN in an ordinary email. If the agency accepts secure upload or in-person verification, prefer that.  
- If you must transmit sensitive documents electronically, confirm the agency’s secure upload method (e.g., an HTTPS portal) before sending.  
- Keep copies of everything you send and note tracking numbers for mailed documents.

